meta {
  name: finish
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/rotate/finish
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{sessionToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "registrationRecord": "<base64 output of a real OpaqueClient.registerFinish() for the NEW password -- see ../README.md>"
  }
}

docs {
  As shipped, this assumes Factor-1-only (no hardened mode) -- the
  account from opaque-bruno-fixture.mjs's default run qualifies, so this
  should succeed with just the body above.

  To exercise Factor 2 (hardened mode): the account must have been
  registered with a continuitySecret (see auth/register-finish's docs),
  and this body needs a "continuitySignature" field: base64 of
  HMAC-SHA256(key = that continuitySecret, data = {{continuityChallenge}}
  from rotation/start). Computing that inside Bruno needs
  require('crypto') in a pre-request script (supported in recent Bruno
  versions) -- not wired here by default since this collection has no
  reason to persist a raw continuitySecret. If your Bruno version's
  script sandbox doesn't expose require('crypto'), compute the HMAC with
  a one-off `node -e` command instead and paste the base64 result in by
  hand.

  Calling this twice with the SAME registrationRecord that already
  landed is intentionally idempotent (see rotation.service.ts) -- it
  returns {"rotated": true} again without requiring a fresh challenge.
}
